📌 Project Overview

This project implements a Campus Event Management System using Java and Object-Oriented Programming principles.

Phase 1 includes the complete implementation of:
- 1.1 User Management
- 1.2 Event Management
- 1.3 Booking Management
- 1.4 Waitlist Management

The system allows administrators to manage users, create and maintain events, process bookings, enforce capacity rules, and maintain waitlists using a menu-driven console interface.
-All data is stored in memory (no database).-

1) Modules and Features

1.1 User Management
The User Management module maintains the system’s user registry and provides the identity layer required for booking operations.
Supported User Types
         - Student
         - Staff
         - Guest
User Attributes
         - userId (unique)
         - name
         - email
         - userType
Features
- Create a user (prevent duplicate userIds)
- View user details (including confirmed bookings summary)
- List all users in readable format

1.2 Event Management
The Event Management module handles the creation and administration of campus events.
Supported Event Types
               - Workshop
               - Seminar
               - Concert
Common Event Attributes
               - eventId (unique)
               - title
               - dateTime
               - location
               - capacity (must be > 0)
               - status (Active / Cancelled)
Type-Specific Fields
               - Workshop → topic
               - Seminar → speakerName
               - Concert → ageRestriction (display only)
Features
- Create an event (validate capacity and prevent duplicate eventIds)
- Update event details while maintaining valid state
- Cancel an event:
All confirmed and waitlisted bookings become Cancelled
Waitlist is cleared
- List all events
- Search by title (partial and case-insensitive)
- Filter by event type

1.3 Booking Management
The Booking Management module connects users to events while enforcing capacity and policy rules.
Booking Attributes
              - bookingId (unique)
              - userId
              - eventId
              - createdAt
              - bookingStatus (Confirmed / Waitlisted / Cancelled)

Booking Rules
- A user cannot book the same event twice.
- If capacity is available → booking is Confirmed.
- If event is full → booking is Waitlisted.
- If a confirmed booking is cancelled → first waitlisted booking is promoted automatically.

Booking limits:
- Student → max 3 Confirmed bookings
- Staff → max 5 Confirmed bookings
- Guest → max 1 Confirmed booking
- Concert ageRestriction is informational only (not enforced).

Features
- Book an event (enforce all rules)
- Cancel a booking (with automatic promotion logic)
- View a user’s bookings
- View event roster:
      Confirmed list
      Waitlist (correct order)

1.4 Waitlist Management
The Waitlist Management module ensures correct first-come, first-served behavior.
Features
- Add booking to waitlist when event is full
- Maintain correct order of waitlisted users
- View waitlist with user details and timestamps
- Remove from waitlist upon cancellation
- Automatically promote first waitlisted booking when:
      A confirmed booking is cancelled, or
      Capacity increases
- Prevent duplicate waitlist entries
- Clear waitlist when event is cancelled


The system demonstrates:
- Encapsulation (private fields with getters/setters)
- Inheritance (User and Event subclasses)
- Abstraction (base classes for shared structure)
- Polymorphism (handling users/events through base types)
- Proper use of collections (ArrayList, Queue)

Assumptions
- Data is stored in memory only.
- The system is admin-operated.
- No external libraries or database connections are used.

               
How to Run the Program
1) Open the project in IntelliJ (or any Java IDE).
2) Ensure all files are inside the src directory.
3) Run src/main/java/UI/MainUI.java.
4) Use the console menu to navigate through system features.









